{"id": "tea:manace-sloka:2", "source": "src:manace-sloka", "location": {"ref": "śloka 2"}, "paraphrase": "O good mind, go by the path of devotion; then Śrī Hari is reached of himself. Give up all that the world rightly blames; do with a full heart all that it rightly honours.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "seeker", "naya": null, "path": ["devotion"], "stage": "beginner"}, "types": ["practice", "ethics"], "original": {"text": "मना सज्जना भक्तिपंथेंचि जावें । तरी श्रीहरी पाविजे तो स्वभावें ॥", "script": "Devanāgarī", "edition": "recalled from memory; to be checked against a printed edition", "licence": "public domain (pre-1900 text)"}, "teachers": ["tch:samartha-ramdas"], "concepts": ["cpt:mind-instructed"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "ai_translated": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U26-regional-bhakti"], "disagreements": []}, "coverage": ["A9"], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U26-regional-bhakti"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:manace-sloka:3", "source": "src:manace-sloka", "location": {"ref": "śloka 3 (number approximate)"}, "paraphrase": "At dawn let the mind think of Rāma; let speech utter Rāma first of all.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "seeker", "naya": null, "path": ["sound", "devotion"], "stage": "beginner"}, "types": ["practice"], "original": {"text": "प्रभातें मनीं राम चिंतीत जावा । पुढें वैखरी राम आधीं वदावा ॥", "script": "Devanāgarī", "edition": "recalled from memory; to be checked against a printed edition", "licence": "public domain (pre-1900 text)"}, "teachers": ["tch:samartha-ramdas"], "concepts": ["cpt:divine-name", "cpt:mind-instructed"], "practices": ["prc:rama-nama-japa"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "ai_translated": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U26-regional-bhakti"], "disagreements": []}, "coverage": ["A9"], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U26-regional-bhakti"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:manace-sloka:jagi-sarva-sukhi", "source": "src:manace-sloka", "location": {"ref": "śloka c. 11 (number to verify)"}, "paraphrase": "Who in the world is wholly happy? Inquire, O mind, and search it out yourself; what you did before, you now reap.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "causal", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "beginner"}, "types": ["world-fate", "karma-liberation"], "original": {"text": "जगीं सर्व सुखी असा कोण आहे । विचारें मना तूंचि शोधूनि पाहे ॥", "script": "Devanāgarī", "edition": "recalled from memory; to be checked against a printed edition", "licence": "public domain (pre-1900 text)"}, "teachers": ["tch:samartha-ramdas"], "concepts": ["cpt:mind-instructed", "cpt:vairagya"], "terms": ["trm:karma"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "ai_translated": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U26-regional-bhakti"], "disagreements": []}, "coverage": ["A9"], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U26-regional-bhakti"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
